        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: naufragium, naufragiī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "naufragium, naufragiī — \"a shipwreck\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Naufragium prope lītus factum est. A shipwreck happened near the shore."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter, built from the words for 'ship' and 'to break'. Naufragium facere: to be shipwrecked."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "naufragium stands for an older nāvifragium, from nāvis, \"ship\", and frangō, \"to break\" (Lewis & Short): a ship-breaking."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
