          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: mergō, mergere",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mergō, mergere — \"to sink, to plunge, to dip\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Undae nāvem parvam mersērunt. The waves sank the little ship."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mergō, mergere, mersī, mersum. English merge and submerge come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mergō is an inherited verb that Lewis & Short connect with a Sanskrit verb meaning \"to dip\". English merge, submerge and immerse come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
